  "body": "Part of #4023. Follow-up of #4254. It is delivered on `side/path-kernel` (AGENTS.md **Side branch**).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe fix of #4254 lets a stay-down link end with an approach from the air: a straight stretch from the air to the start of an open piece on the stock edge. The proof makes sure that the approach cuts no stock off the planned curve.\n\nThe approach can arrive at full width. On the dog bone (motion pin `kernel_order_and_link_round_the_disc_and_the_dog_bone`, Outside), one approach arrives at full width at (-2.40, 25.00) on the top stock edge. For its last tool radius the disc cuts as a slot (180 degrees). The reading goes from `worst 167, full 0` to `worst 180, full 1`.\n\nThe load stage (K3) reads the cuts. It does not read the links. Thus no stage names or slows this full-width stretch.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Let the load stage (or the link stage) read the engagement of the approach stretch of a stay link.\n- Name the full-width stretch, or slow the feed on it, as K3 does for a full-width stretch of a cut.\n- Alternatively, prove an approach that arrives with less engagement, for example an approach that comes in along a stretch that a cut already made has cleared.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe full-width approach on the dog bone is named or slowed by the plan, and the motion pin reads it. No new constant makes stock open.\n",
